    "fedya": "anja"
  },
  "labels": {
    "anya": "Сеня",
    "fedya": "Федя"
  },
  "segments": [
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "In the kitchen of Claude Monet, Senya prepares to eat a leather belt after losing a bet to Fedya. Fedya mocks him by telling him to tenderize the leather first so it is not as tough as Senya's steak from yesterday.",
      "gap": 0.8
    },
    {
      "v": "fedya",
      "t": "Сеня, ты уже принёс этот ремень?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "fedya",
      "t": "Только весь сразу один не ешь!",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "fedya",
      "t": "Оставь и мне маленький кусочек.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Очень смешно ты сегодня шутишь.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Я его сначала мелко нарежу ножом.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "А потом спокойно всё съем.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "fedya",
      "t": "Да, ты всё правильно придумал.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "fedya",
      "t": "Только отбей его хорошо сначала!",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "fedya",
      "t": "Иначе он будет очень жёсткий.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "fedya",
      "t": "Прямо как твой вчерашний стейк!",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Мои мясные блюда всегда вкусные!",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Отстань от меня, ты понял?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "fedya",
      "t": "Понял, желаю тебе приятного аппетита!",
      "gap": 0.9
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "Listen to Fedya teasing Senya in the kitchen over their bet.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "fedya",
      "t": "Сеня, ты уже принёс этот ремень?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Senya, did you already bring that belt?' Fedya turns a statement into a question purely through rising intonation on the word meaning 'already', pairing it with 'brought' and 'belt'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "fedya",
      "t": "Только весь сразу один не ешь!",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Just do not eat it all at once by yourself!' Fedya leads with the direct command form meaning 'eat', combining 'only' with 'at once' and 'one'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "fedya",
      "t": "Оставь и мне маленький кусочек.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Leave a small piece for me too.' Fedya leads with the direct command form meaning 'keep', pairing it with 'short' and 'slice'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Очень смешно ты сегодня шутишь.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'You are joking very amusingly today.' Senya expresses this naturally by combining the word for 'very much' with 'ridiculous' and 'today'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Я его сначала мелко нарежу ножом.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'I will slice it finely with a knife first.' Senya plans to cut the leather into tiny strips.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "А потом спокойно всё съем.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'And then I will calmly eat it all.' The perfective future verb means 'I will eat it all up'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "fedya",
      "t": "Да, ты всё правильно придумал.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Yes, you thought of everything rightly.' The phrasing opens with 'right' before bringing in 'came up with' to make the point clear.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "fedya",
      "t": "Только отбей его хорошо сначала!",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Just tenderize it well first!' The imperative refers to pounding meat with a kitchen mallet.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "fedya",
      "t": "Иначе он будет очень жёсткий.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Otherwise it will be very tough.' Fedya warns that the leather will be hard to chew.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "fedya",
      "t": "Прямо как твой вчерашний стейк!",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Just like your steak from yesterday!' Russian omits the present-tense verb 'to be' here, linking 'right' directly with 'how', combining 'right' with 'how' and 'yesterday's'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Мои мясные блюда всегда вкусные!",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'My meat dishes are always delicious!' As the meat chef, Senya proudly defends his steaks.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Отстань от меня, ты понял?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Leave me alone, did you understand?' Senya leads with the direct command form meaning 'leave alone', followed by 'understood?'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "fedya",
      "t": "Понял, желаю тебе приятного аппетита!",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Got it, I wish you a good appetite!' Fedya leaves him with a parting joke. Now listen to the kitchen banter between Senya and Fedya again. Now let's listen to the whole conversation again from start to finish.",
      "gap": 0.9
    },
    {
      "v": "fedya",
      "t": "Сеня, ты уже принёс этот ремень?",
      "gap": 0.5
    },
